2-04. Leather-faced work gloves.--Leather-faced work gloves shall be worn when;
(a) Handling wire rope;

(b) Handling sharp or rough steel or rock.
(c) Sand blasting;
(d) Handling molten metal (ie) babbit, etc;
(e) The work being done requires protection greater than that afforded by cotton gloves.
2-05. Rubber gloves shall be worn when:
(a) Using creosote, caustic or acids;
(b) Working with electricity - power lines or utility lines at locks where cut-off is not available. No work
should be conducted unless authorized by the supervisors.
